{
 "system": "adaptintake",
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Hello, I'm here to help you get ready for your appointment. Could you tell me what has been bothering you?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "It's burning when I pass water."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Could you tell me when you first noticed the burning when you pass water, how it came on, and if you have any allergies or bad reactions to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "It started about four days ago."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Could you tell me how much this burning is affecting you, and what medicines you take or have taken recently?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "The stinging is about five out of ten."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Could you tell me a bit about your health in the past — for example, any ongoing conditions, past illnesses, operations, or hospital stays?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I have an underactive thyroid."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Do you have any allergies or bad reactions to medicines — yes, no, or are you not sure?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, trimethoprim gave me a rash."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Have you noticed any other symptoms along with the burning when you pass water?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "The water looks cloudy."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Are you taking any medicines at the moment — for example, regular ones or anything new or changed recently — yes, no, or are you not sure?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I take levothyroxine every morning."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Where do you feel the burning when you pass water?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "Just when I go, really. My niece brought me here today."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Does anything make the burning better or worse?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I haven't noticed anything helping it."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Is the burning there every time you pass water, or does it come and go?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "It's there every time I go."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "What worries you most about the burning when you pass water?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I hope to get antibiotics before the weekend."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You mentioned an underactive thyroid — is there anything else about your past health, such as other long-term conditions, past illnesses, operations, or hospital stays, that you’d like to add?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I had a water infection about a year ago."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Has the burning when you pass water changed anything about your usual daily activities?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I've stopped going to the coffee morning."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Besides your urine looking cloudy, is there anything else you've noticed along with the burning when you pass water?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "It smells stronger too."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Apart from your underactive thyroid and the water infection you had about a year ago, is there anything else about your past health you’d like to add?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I have thin bones."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Besides your Levothyroxine, is there anything else you’d like to add about any other medicines you take, including new or changed ones?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I take a tablet once a week for my bones."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Besides those, is there anything else you've noticed?"
  },
  {
   "role": "patient",
   "text": "I use a cream from the hospital. Can't recall the name."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, that is very helpful. I have put together a short summary of what you told me. Please read it and tell me if anything should be corrected before it goes to your doctor."
  }
 ],
